# PART 1: PRIOR ART SEARCH RESULTS

## Class 3: DXVR Spatial Synchronization

### What We Found

**Dead reckoning / predictive interpolation is NOT novel.** It has been used in multiplayer games since 1996:

| Technique | First Use | Source |
|-----------|-----------|--------|
| Position + velocity extrapolation (dead reckoning) | 1996 | QuakeWorld, DIS IEEE standard |
| Position + velocity + acceleration extrapolation | 2004+ | Hanawa & Yonekura (Taylor expansion) |
| Client-side prediction | 1996 | QuakeWorld |
| Interpolation between states | 2001 | Half-Life, Age of Empires |
| Incoming delay buffer | 2001 | Half-Life |
| Time warp | 2001 | Half-Life |
| Jitter-adaptive interpolation | 2014+ | Savery & Graham toolkit |
| Machine learning for prediction | 2016+ | Henze et al. (ANN touch prediction) |

**Key ACM Survey (2022):** "A Survey and Taxonomy of Latency Compensation Techniques for Network Computer Games" — catalogs **85+ peer-reviewed papers** on latency compensation, divided into 4 classes (feedback, prediction, time manipulation, world adjustment) and 11 technique types. The most popular categories are extrapolation and incoming delay.

**What IS potentially novel in DXVR:**

The individual techniques are well-known, but the **specific combination** may be novel:

1. **Hierarchical spatial partitioning for progressive delta transmission** — dead reckoning papers use flat position/velocity vectors, not hierarchical room→object→vertex granularity
2. **Temporal coherence mesh with weighted LWW by device authority** — standard LWW is unweighted; weighting by tracking precision (6DoF vs 3DoF) is not found in surveyed literature
3. **Network partition recovery via three-way merge with monotonic sequence numbers** — standard systems freeze or disconnect on partition; three-way merge with sequence-number-based replay is not in the 85-paper survey
4. **Hardware-aware rendering that adjusts quality based on GPU compute, FOV, and refresh rate** — most systems render at fixed quality; adaptive rendering based on full capability profile is less common in multiplayer sync literature

**Verdict after search:** DXVR is **fileable** but claims must be narrowly scoped to the specific combinations above. Broad claims on "predictive interpolation" will be rejected.

